    "sloc": 13,
    "title": "One Portable Tensor-Core Kernel",
    "description": "13-line Crisp matmul that runs unchanged on B200, H100, A100 and L4 and is bit-exact against cuBLAS: `matrix-multiply-tile-stride` walks output tiles and K, `load-tile` stages A and B slices, `mma-accumulate-via-tile` accumulates in f32 on the tensor cores, and `(store-tile (to-half C-tile) ...)` rounds to fp16 as it stores",
    "idioms": [
      "matrix-multiply-tile-stride: output-tile walk + K walk + epilogue in one form",
      "make-register-tile: an f32 accumulator that lives in registers",
      "mma-accumulate-via-tile (16 8 16): fp16 tensor-core MMA from staged shared-memory tiles",
      "(store-tile (to-half C-tile) C ...): fused round-to-nearest narrowing on the store (endeavour 196)"
    ],
